    "id": "l3a",
    "topic": "Урок 3 · работа из дома",
    "title": "Max Works for Himself",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Max is a marketer. Two years ago, he left his office job and applied for jobs at big companies. There was so much competition! Luckily, a friend said: \"Why don't you work for yourself?\"",
      "Now Max works for himself. He works from home, and his flat is his safe space. Every Sunday he plans his whole week and sets time for each task. He starts work at nine in the morning and has six tasks a day.",
      "His workspace is simple: a laptop, headphones and a wireless mouse. He is often on calls with clients. Sometimes he forgets to turn on his microphone, and a client says: \"Max, you're muted!\"",
      "Working from home isn't always easy. Max doesn't have to go to the office, so he hardly moves. He has to remind himself to move around. Sometimes he looks out of the window and says: \"Oh, when did the sun go down?\" His plants are his only co-workers.",
      "Now he has a flexible schedule. He works out twice a week and takes time off when he needs it. He doesn't earn a lot of money yet, but he is grateful. \"It suits me,\" he says. \"Sorry, I'm on a call in five. Wish me luck!\""
    ],
